Adds TikTok-style hook text overlay to a 1080x1920 clip using ffmpeg drawtext filter.

Exports:
```typescript
export interface OverlayOptions {
  hookText: string;          // brief.hook (5-8 words)
  hookDuration?: number;     // seconds to show hook (default: 4)
  fontSize?: number;         // default: 82
  fontColor?: string;        // default: 'white'
  borderWidth?: number;      // default: 4 (black stroke)
}

export async function applyTextOverlay(
  inputPath: string,
  outputPath: string,
  opts: OverlayOptions
): Promise<void>;
```

Implementation:
1. Word-wrap hookText at ~20 chars per line (split at word boundaries)
2. Write wrapped text to a temp file (e.g. /tmp/hook_{hash}.txt) to avoid ffmpeg escaping issues
3. Build drawtext filter:
   ```
   drawtext=
     fontfile=/System/Library/Fonts/Supplemental/Impact.ttf:
     textfile={tmpFile}:
     fontsize=82:
     fontcolor=white:
     borderw=4:
     bordercolor=black:
     line_spacing=8:
     x=(w-text_w)/2:
     y=(h/2)-180:
     enable='between(t,0,{hookDuration})'
   ```
4. Apply via fluent-ffmpeg using .complexFilter or .videoFilter
5. Copy audio stream unchanged (-c:a copy)
6. H.264 video re-encode with crf 20, preset fast
7. Clean up temp file after render

Word-wrap helper:
```typescript
function wrapHook(text: string, maxChars = 20): string {
  const words = text.split(' ');
  const lines: string[] = [];
  let cur = '';
  for (const w of words) {
    if (cur.length + w.length + 1 > maxChars && cur) {
      lines.push(cur.trim());
      cur = w + ' ';
    } else {
      cur += w + ' ';
    }
  }
  if (cur.trim()) lines.push(cur.trim());
  return lines.join('\n');
}
```

Max 65 lines.

